Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:06.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Randomly masking and predicting tokens has powered pretraining in language modeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.10,0:00:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper, Uni-MASK,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.50,0:00:11.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}shows the same idea applies naturally to sequential decision making.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.03,0:00:16.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Many well-studied tasks, behavior cloning, offline reinforcement learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.96,0:00:19.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}inverse dynamics, and waypoint conditioning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.89,0:00:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}all correspond to different maskings over a sequence of states, actions, and returns.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.56,0:00:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Uni-MASK unifies them into one framework,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.29,0:00:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a single model trained this way often matches or beats specialized single-task models,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.28,0:00:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and consistently outperforms them after fine-tuning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.05,0:00:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In sequential decision making, tasks like behavior cloning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.93,0:00:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}offline reinforcement learning, inverse dynamics,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.16,0:00:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and goal or waypoint conditioning are typically each handled by a separate,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.10,0:00:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}specially trained model.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.68,0:00:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Yet all of these tasks operate over the very same object: a trajectory of states,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.01,0:00:58.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}actions, and returns.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.39,0:01:05.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Training a distinct model per task ignores this shared structure and misses the chance to build richer,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.17,0:01:07.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reusable representations across tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.97,0:01:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Masked language modeling, the technique behind BERT,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.30,0:01:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}trains models to predict randomly masked tokens in a sequence,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.27,0:01:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}producing rich bidirectional representations that transfer to many tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.95,0:01:24.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors observe that this idea maps directly onto decision making.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.44,0:01:28.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}If you treat states and actions as tokens and mask the last action,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.73,0:01:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}predicting it is exactly a behavior cloning inference.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.19,0:01:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Different tasks are simply different masking patterns over the same trajectory,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.25,0:01:42.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so a single masked-prediction objective can, in principle, express them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.42,0:01:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The main contribution is the Uni-MASK framework,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.62,0:01:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a unified way to specify models for sequential decision making by casting each inference
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.49,0:01:54.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}task as a masking scheme over a trajectory of states,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.03,0:01:57.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}actions, and reward-to-go tokens.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.23,0:01:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because tasks are just maskings,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.36,0:02:04.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a single model can be trained to perform behavior cloning, reward conditioning,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.63,0:02:08.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}dynamics modeling, and goal or waypoint conditioning together.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.77,0:02:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors show this single model often matches or exceeds specialized single-task models,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.84,0:02:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and consistently outperforms them after fine-tuning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.31,0:02:23.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Along the way they also introduce Decision-GPT, an improved GPT-based baseline.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.88,0:02:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Uni-MASK represents a trajectory as a sequence of per-timestep tokens: a state,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.01,0:02:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}an action, and optionally a property token such as return-to-go,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.16,0:02:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the sum of future rewards.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.85,0:02:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A masking scheme specifies two things: which input tokens are visible to the model,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.24,0:02:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and which output tokens the model must predict and be scored on.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.40,0:02:47.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Different schemes recover different tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.12,0:02:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Behavior cloning conditions on past states and actions and predicts the next action;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.58,0:02:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}goal conditioning additionally reveals a future state;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.08,0:02:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reward conditioning reveals return-to-go.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.75,0:03:05.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The model itself is a bidirectional BERT-style transformer encoder that stacks each timestep's state,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.30,0:03:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}action, and property into one vector and predicts the masked tokens.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.72,0:03:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors compare four training regimes: single-task,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.29,0:03:17.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}multi-task with a random scheme per snippet, fully random masking,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.57,0:03:21.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and random-mask pretraining followed by task-specific fine-tuning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.16,0:03:25.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The framework is evaluated on two environments.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.28,0:03:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The first is MiniGrid,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.74,0:03:31.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a gridworld where an agent must reach a fixed goal behind a locked door;
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.52,0:03:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it is used to qualitatively demonstrate the many inference tasks a single model can perform
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.56,0:03:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and to compare task-specific validation losses.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.68,0:03:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The second is Maze2D, a continuous-control maze from the MuJoCo-based D4RL benchmark,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.32,0:03:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}where the authors measure test-time reward over one thousand rollouts across five seeds,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.17,0:03:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}comparing Uni-MASK against a feedforward network, Decision Transformer,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.88,0:04:02.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and their own improved Decision-GPT baseline at context lengths of five and ten.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.49,0:04:04.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In the MiniGrid environment,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.27,0:04:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a single model trained with random masking outperforms single-task models on all tasks,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.78,0:04:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and adding task-specific fine-tuning on top of random-mask pretraining gives the best performance of all,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.44,0:04:20.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}beating single-task models on every task except behavior cloning.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.56,0:04:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This means that even if you only care about one inference task,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.56,0:04:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}first training on many tasks generally helps.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.41,0:04:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In the harder Maze2D environment,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.50,0:04:35.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}fine-tuning becomes critical: the fine-tuned Uni-MASK models reach rewards around two point seven,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.72,0:04:38.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}outperforming every baseline at context length five,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.02,0:04:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}including a Decision Transformer that scores only around one point one to one point five.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.96,0:04:49.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The training-regime comparison isolates the effect of each ingredient and shows fine-tuning
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.80,0:04:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}is the decisive one for good performance in the more complex Maze2D environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.64,0:04:59.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A second,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.49,0:05:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}controlled comparison pits single-task Uni-MASK against the Decision-GPT baseline,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.33,0:05:09.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}where the only real difference is a BERT-style versus a GPT-style backbone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.17,0:05:13.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Here the picture is nuanced: BERT works well at a short context length of five,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.01,0:05:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but at length ten the BERT-style Uni-MASK models degrade and are outbeaten by the GPT-based Decision-GPT,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.86,0:05:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}revealing a known difficulty of BERT-like architectures with longer-sequence generation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.00,0:05:26.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture the impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.19,0:05:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In Maze2D at context length five,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.38,0:05:34.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the fine-tuned Uni-MASK models reach reward around two point seven three on both behavior
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.30,0:05:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}cloning and reward conditioning,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.42,0:05:42.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}compared to just one point one three and one point four nine for the Decision Transformer,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.40,0:05:47.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and around one point five to one point seven for a feedforward network.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.12,0:05:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}These results are averaged over five seeds and one thousand rollouts.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.70,0:05:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And critically, a single Uni-MASK model handles behavior cloning,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.02,0:05:58.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reward conditioning, dynamics modeling,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.61,0:06:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and goal and waypoint conditioning all at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.03,0:06:07.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lasting takeaway is simple and powerful: many seemingly distinct sequential-decision
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.60,0:06:11.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}tasks are just different maskings of the same trajectory,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.21,0:06:15.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so a single masked-prediction model can replace a zoo of specialized ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.89,0:06:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And training on many masking schemes, then fine-tuning,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.37,0:06:23.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}generally does better than training on any single task alone,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.23,0:06:25.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}even when you only care about that one task.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.01,0:06:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The main caveat is architectural,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.10,0:06:33.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}BERT-style models shine at short contexts but struggle to generate over longer sequences,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.73,0:06:39.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}suggesting that combining GPT-style backbones with random masking is a promising next step.
